{
  "text": "On this day, September 23rd: In 1999: Qantas Flight 1 overruns a runway in Bangkok during a storm, causing minor injuries to some passengers. In 1956: A tropical storm originating in the eastern Pacific Ocean passes into the Gulf of Mexico and is upgraded and named Hurricane Flossy just hours before striking the Gulf Coast and causing 15 deaths and an estimated US$24.8 million in damages. And in 1905: Norway and Sweden sign the Karlstad Treaty, peacefully dissolving the Union between the two countries.",
